.Dd April 27, 2026
.Dt RE 4D
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm re
.Nd Realtek RTL8125/RTL8126/RTL8127 Ethernet driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /dev/net/re*
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver is a GLDv3 NIC driver for modern Realtek PCIe Ethernet
controllers.
Supported devices include:
.Bl -bullet
.It
RTL8125 2.5GbE controllers
.It
RTL8126 5GbE controllers
.It
RTL8127 10GbE controllers
.El
.Pp
The driver supports checksum offload, MSI/MSI-X interrupts, multiple
RX/TX queues, RSS, jumbo frames, auto-negotiation, and pause frames.
Jumbo frames are supported up to 9216 bytes.
.Pp
A device instance is exposed as
.Pa /dev/net/re0 ,
.Pa /dev/net/re1 ,
and so on.
The device supports
.Xr dlpi 4P
and can be used through
.Xr libdlpi 3LIB .
.Sh LINK CONFIGURATION
Link configuration is managed using
.Xr dladm 8 .
.Pp
Auto-negotiation is always enabled.
Link speed is determined by the advertised capabilities of the
controller and link partner.
Supported link speeds depend on the controller, link partner, and
cabling.
.Sh INTERRUPTS
The driver supports MSI-X interrupts and falls back to MSI when MSI-X
resources are not available.
MSI-X allows per-queue interrupt handling and is the preferred mode.
.Sh TIMER INTERRUPT MODE
The driver provides an optional timer-based interrupt mode configured in
.Pa re.conf .
.Pp
In this mode, the device generates interrupts periodically.
This mode is intended as a fallback for systems where regular device
interrupts are missed or unreliable.
.Pp
The
.Sy timer_count
property controls the interrupt interval.
Higher values reduce the interrupt rate, and lower values increase it.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
Driver settings are configured in
.Pa /kernel/drv/re.conf .
.Pp
Supported properties:
.Bl -tag -width Sy
.It Sy force_msi
Force MSI/MSI-X interrupt mode.
The default value is 0.
.It Sy timer_int_enable
Enable timer interrupt mode.
The default value is 0.
.It Sy timer_count
Set the timer interrupt interval.
Higher values reduce the interrupt rate.
.El
.Sh TEMPERATURE MONITORING
Some controllers provide a temperature sensor exposed through FMA.
Temperature monitoring is supported on RTL8125B and newer devices.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa /kernel/drv/amd64/re
Device driver
.It Pa /kernel/drv/re.conf
Driver configuration
.It Pa /dev/net/re*
Device nodes
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libdlpi 3LIB ,
.Xr dlpi 4P ,
.Xr dladm 8
